================================================================================
                    GLOWIFY AUTOMATION PROJECT
                    COMPLETE WORKFLOW EXPLANATION
================================================================================

PROJECT OVERVIEW
================================================================================
The Glowify Automation Framework is an END-TO-END TEST AUTOMATION SYSTEM for 
the Glowify Cosmetics e-commerce website. It simulates real user interactions 
by automating a complete shopping journey from home page to payment gateway.

TECHNOLOGY STACK
================================================================================
• Python 3                    - Programming language
• Selenium WebDriver          - Browser automation tool
• Pytest                      - Test execution framework
• Allure Reports              - Test reporting tool
• Chrome WebDriver            - Browser driver
• Page Object Model (POM)     - Design pattern


COMPLETE EXECUTION FLOW
================================================================================

PHASE 1: PROJECT SETUP & INITIALIZATION
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. USER RUNS TEST COMMAND
   └─> Opens terminal and executes:
       $ pytest tests/test_e2e_flow.py -v

2. PYTEST STARTS
   └─> Pytest discovers test files in "tests" folder
   └─> Reads configuration from pytest.ini
   └─> Reads configuration from conftest.py

3. CONFTEST.PY LOADS
   └─> Registers the "get_driver" fixture
   └─> Sets up the pytest_runtest_makereport hook
   └─> Makes them available to all tests

4. CONFIGURATION LOADS
   └─> config/config.py is read (BASE_URL, BROWSER type)
   └─> Settings stored in memory for use during test


PHASE 2: TEST INITIALIZATION (Before Test Starts)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. FIXTURE EXECUTION: get_driver()
   └─> conftest.py's get_driver fixture runs BEFORE the test
   └─> Line: driver = driver_init()

2. DRIVER FACTORY CREATES BROWSER
   └─> Calls utils/driver_factory.py → get_driver()
   └─> Creates ChromeOptions object with settings
   └─> Adds "--start-maximized" argument (full window size)
   └─> Uses ChromeDriverManager() to auto-download Chrome driver
   └─> Creates webdriver.Chrome() instance
   └─> RESULT: A fully functional Chrome browser ready to use

3. BROWSER LAUNCHED
   └─> Chrome browser window opens (automated)
   └─> Browser is MAXIMIZED for better visibility
   └─> Browser instance stored in "driver" variable
   └─> Yielded to test function via fixture


PHASE 3: TEST EXECUTION STARTS
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

TEST: test_full_user_journey(get_driver)
└─> driver = get_driver (receives active Chrome browser)
└─> Creates instances of all page objects:
    ├─ HomePage(driver)         → home variable
    ├─ ProductListPage(driver)  → product_list variable
    ├─ ProductDetailPage(driver) → product_detail variable
    ├─ CartPage(driver)         → cart variable
    ├─ LoginPage(driver)        → login variable
    ├─ SignupPage(driver)       → signup variable
    └─ CheckoutPage(driver)     → checkout variable

Each page object:
├─> Stores the driver reference
├─> Creates a WebDriverWait object (10-20 second timeout)
├─> Defines element locators (XPath, CSS selectors)
└─> Ready to interact with website


PHASE 4: STEP-BY-STEP TEST EXECUTION
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 1: OPEN HOME PAGE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: home.open()

Processing:
├─> Calls HomePage.open()
├─> Executes: driver.get("https://glowify-cosmetics-site.onrender.com/")
├─> Browser navigates to website URL
├─> Page loads in Chrome browser
├─> HTML, CSS, JavaScript all loaded
├─> Page rendering completes
└─> Browser now shows Glowify home page with products

What User Sees:
└─> Home page displays with navigation menu, products, profile icon


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 2: NAVIGATE TO LIPSTICKS CATEGORY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: home.go_to_lipsticks()

Processing:
1. Creates ActionChains object for mouse movements
2. Waits for Shop menu element to be visible:
   └─> Locator: (By.XPATH, "//a[contains(text(),'Shop')]")
   └─> XPath finds the element containing text "Shop"
   └─> Waits UP TO 20 seconds for it to appear
   └─> If doesn't appear: TEST FAILS with timeout error

3. Hovers mouse over Shop menu:
   └─> ActionChains.move_to_element(shop_element)
   └─> perform() executes the hover action
   └─> Dropdown menu appears (CSS shows hidden menu items)

4. Waits for Lipsticks option in dropdown:
   └─> Locator: (By.XPATH, "//a[contains(@href,'lipsticks')]")
   └─> Waits for dropdown item with href containing "lipsticks"
   └─> Waits UP TO 20 seconds

5. Clicks Lipsticks menu item:
   └─> Calls .click() on the element
   └─> Browser navigates to Lipsticks product page
   └─> Page loads lipsticks category products

What User Sees:
└─> Lipsticks product list page with thumbnails, prices, ratings


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 3: SELECT FIRST PRODUCT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: product_list.select_first_product()

Processing:
1. Calls ProductListPage.select_first_product()
2. Waits for first product link to be clickable:
   └─> Locator: (By.CSS_SELECTOR, ".product-card a")
   └─> CSS selector finds first <a> tag inside .product-card div
   └─> Waits UP TO 10 seconds for element to be clickable

3. Clicks the first product:
   └─> .click() executes on the found element
   └─> Browser navigates to product detail page

What User Sees:
└─> Product detail page with: large image, description, price, 
    reviews, "Add to Cart" button


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 4: ADD PRODUCT TO CART
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: product_detail.add_product_to_cart()

Processing:
1. Waits for page to fully load:
   └─> Executes JavaScript: "document.readyState"
   └─> Waits until value equals "complete"
   └─> Ensures all resources (CSS, JS, images) loaded

2. Finds "Add to Cart" button:
   └─> Locator: (By.CSS_SELECTOR, "button.add-cart")
   └─> Finds first button with class "add-cart"

3. Scrolls button into view:
   └─> "scrollIntoView(true)" JavaScript command
   └─> Scrolls page so button is visible
   └─> Prevents hidden element click errors

4. Clicks "Add to Cart" using JavaScript:
   └─> Regular click might fail due to overlay/disabled state
   └─> Uses: driver.execute_script("arguments[0].click();", btn)
   └─> JavaScript click forces click action
   └─> Product added to cart in database/session

What Happens Backend:
└─> Server receives add-to-cart request
└─> Server updates shopping cart session
└─> Server returns success response
└─> Frontend shows success message or updates cart count


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 5: NAVIGATE TO SHOPPING CART
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: product_detail.go_to_cart()

Processing:
1. Tries to click "Go to Cart" button:
   └─> Locator: (By.XPATH, "//button[contains(@class,'added')]...")
   └─> Looks for dynamic button that appears after adding product
   └─> Waits for it to be clickable

2. If "Go to Cart" fails, clicks cart icon (fallback):
   └─> Locator: (By.CSS_SELECTOR, ".cart-icon a")
   └─> Fallback in case dynamic button doesn't appear

3. Navigates directly to cart URL:
   └─> driver.get("https://glowify-cosmetics-site.onrender.com/shop/cart/")
   └─> Always navigates to cart URL to ensure we're there
   └─> Guarantees we reach cart page even if clicks fail

What User Sees:
└─> Shopping cart page showing:
    - Added product with image, price, quantity
    - Total price calculation
    - "Proceed to Checkout" button


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 6: PROCEED TO CHECKOUT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: cart.proceed_to_checkout()

Processing:
1. Checks if we're on cart page:
   └─> "cart" in self.driver.current_url
   └─> If not on cart page, navigate to it

2. Waits for page to fully load:
   └─> Executes: "document.readyState"
   └─> Waits for value "complete"

3. Finds Checkout button:
   └─> Locator: (By.CSS_SELECTOR, "a.checkout-btn")
   └─> Waits UP TO 20 seconds for button

4. Scrolls button into view:
   └─> "scrollIntoView(true)" JavaScript
   └─> Makes button visible on screen

5. Clicks Checkout button:
   └─> Try regular click first
   └─> If fails, use JavaScript click

6. Handles redirect scenarios:
   └─> If redirected to login page: checkout fails, returns
   └─> If still on cart page: navigates directly to checkout URL

What User Sees (if logged in):
└─> Checkout page with delivery form fields

What User Sees (if NOT logged in):
└─> Redirected to login/signup page


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 7: CHECK IF USER IS LOGGED IN (SMART CHECK)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: if not home.is_logged_in():

Processing:
1. Calls home.is_logged_in()
2. Waits for profile icon to appear:
   └─> Locator: (By.CSS_SELECTOR, "img, .profile-icon")
   └─> Looks for user profile icon
   └─> Waits UP TO 20 seconds

3. Clicks profile icon:
   └─> Triggers dropdown menu with user options

4. Gets current URL:
   └─> current_url = driver.current_url
   └─> Stored for comparison

5. Checks URL for "login":
   └─> If "login" in URL → User NOT logged in → Return False
   └─> If "login" not in URL → Continue

6. Tries to find logout/orders dropdown:
   └─> Waits for: "Logout" or "My Orders" links
   └─> If found → User IS logged in → Return True
   └─> If NOT found → User NOT logged in → Return False


CASE A: USER IS LOGGED IN
─────────────────────────
└─> is_logged_in() returns True
└─> Skips registration block
└─> Continues to fill checkout details


CASE B: USER NOT LOGGED IN
──────────────────────────
└─> is_logged_in() returns False
└─> Enters if block to register user

Processing sub-steps:

  STEP 7B.1: GO TO SIGNUP PAGE
  ────────────────────────────
  Code: login.go_to_signup()
  
  Processing:
  ├─> Waits for email field (page indicator)
  ├─> Waits for URL to contain "login"
  ├─> Finds Sign Up link
  ├─> Clicks or JavaScript clicks it
  └─> Browser navigates to signup page

  What User Sees:
  └─> Signup form with: name, email, password fields


  STEP 7B.2: REGISTER NEW USER
  ────────────────────────────
  Code: signup.register_user()
  
  Processing:
  1. Fills Name field:
     └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "name")
     └─> Sends "Test User" text
  
  2. Fills Email field:
     └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "email")
     └─> Generates unique email: "test{timestamp}@gmail.com"
     └─> Uses current Unix timestamp for uniqueness
     └─> Each test run uses different email
  
  3. Fills Password field:
     └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "password")
     └─> Sends "Test@123"
  
  4. Clicks Register button:
     └─> Locator: (By.XPATH, "//button[contains(text(),'Register')]")
     └─> Sends registration request to server
  
  What Backend Does:
  └─> Validates form inputs
  └─> Creates new user account
  └─> Hashes password for security
  └─> Stores user in database
  └─> Creates session/auth token for user
  └─> Redirects user to confirmation/home page


  STEP 7B.3: RETURN TO HOME & RE-ADD PRODUCT
  ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Code: home.open() then repeat steps 2-5
  
  Why?
  └─> After registration, cart is cleared (new user = empty cart)
  └─> Must add product again to cart before checkout
  
  Processing:
  ├─> home.open() → Navigate to home page
  ├─> home.go_to_lipsticks() → Browse to lipsticks
  ├─> product_list.select_first_product() → Click product
  ├─> product_detail.add_product_to_cart() → Add to cart
  └─> product_detail.go_to_cart() → Go to cart page


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 8: PROCEED TO CHECKOUT (SECOND TIME)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: cart.proceed_to_checkout()

Processing: (Same as Step 6)
1. Verify on cart page
2. Wait for page load
3. Find and click Checkout button
4. This time: User is logged in, so redirects to checkout form page

What User Sees:
└─> Checkout form page with delivery details


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 9: FILL DELIVERY DETAILS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: checkout.fill_details()

Processing:
1. Waits for First Name field to be visible:
   └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "first_name")
   └─> Sends keys "Test"

2. Fills Mobile field:
   └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "mobile")
