3. Fills Address field:
   └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "address")
   └─> Sends "Chennai"

4. Fills City field:
   └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "city")
   └─> Sends "Chennai"

5. Fills State field:
   └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "state")
   └─> Sends "Tamil Nadu"

6. Fills Pincode field:
   └─> Locator: (By.NAME, "pincode")
   └─> Sends "600001"

What Backend Does:
└─> Validates address information
└─> Calculates shipping cost if applicable
└─> Stores delivery address in order
└─> Prepares order for payment


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 10: SUBMIT ORDER
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: checkout.place_order_click()

Processing:
1. Finds "Place Order" button:
   └─> Locator: (By.ID, "placeOrderBtn")

2. Clicks the button:
   └─> JavaScript click to ensure it works
   └─> Sends order submission request to backend

What Backend Does:
├─> Creates order record with:
│  ├─ User information
│  ├─ Product details
│  ├─ Delivery address
│  └─ Order timestamp
├─> Generates order ID
├─> Creates payment session
├─> Sends Razorpay payment request
└─> Returns payment gateway iframe to frontend

What Frontend Does:
└─> Opens Razorpay payment gateway popup (iframe)
└─> Shows payment form to user


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STEP 11: VERIFY PAYMENT POPUP
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Code: checkout.verify_payment_popup()

Processing:
1. Waits for Razorpay iframe to load:
   └─> Locator: (By.CSS_SELECTOR, "iframe.razorpay-checkout-frame")
   └─> Waits UP TO 20 seconds

2. Switches to iframe:
   └─> driver.switch_to.frame(iframe_element)
   └─> "Switch to frame" = browser context now inside iframe
   └─> Can now interact with payment form elements

3. Payment frame appears:
   └─> Shows credit/debit card input
   └─> Shows payment gateway interface
   └─> TEST STOPS HERE (doesn't complete actual payment)

What This Verifies:
└─> Order reached payment stage successfully ✓
└─> Payment gateway loaded correctly ✓
└─> User can see payment options ✓
└─> TEST PASSES if we can see payment popup ✓


PHASE 5: TEST COMPLETION & REPORTING
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. TEST EXECUTION ENDS
   └─> All steps completed successfully
   └─> Function returns (implicitly returns None)
   └─> Pytest considers test PASSED

2. FIXTURE TEARDOWN: get_driver()
   └─> conftest.py gets control back after yield
   └─> Executes: driver.quit()
   └─> Quits entire Chrome browser and all windows
   └─> Closes browser process

3. TEST REPORT GENERATION
   └─> Pytest marks test as PASSED ✓
   └─> No failure hook triggered (no screenshot needed)
   └─> Records execution time
   └─> Stores result in reports/allure-results

4. PYTEST FINISHES
   └─> Summary output to terminal:
       • Test name
       • Execution time
       • Status (PASSED/FAILED)
   └─> Generates Allure report data


WHAT HAPPENS IF TEST FAILS
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

When any step fails (e.g., element not found):

1. EXCEPTION RAISED
   └─> TimeoutException, NoSuchElementException, etc.
   └─> Test execution stops

2. FAILURE HOOK TRIGGERS
   └─> pytest_runtest_makereport hook activates
   └─> Checks: report.when == "call" and report.failed

3. SCREENSHOT TAKEN
   └─> Gets driver from funcargs
   └─> Creates reports/screenshots/ folder
   └─> Saves screenshot: reports/screenshots/{test_name}.png
   └─> Screenshot shows exact state when test failed

4. ALLURE ATTACHMENT
   └─> Attaches PNG screenshot to Allure report
   └─> Screenshot visible in Allure HTML report

5. DRIVER STILL QUITS
   └─> Finally block ensures driver.quit() runs
   └─> Browser closes properly

6. TEST MARKED FAILED
   └─> Terminal shows: FAILED
   └─> Pytest reports failure


